---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Lightbox from '../components/Lightbox.astro';

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:," />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var saved = localStorage.getItem('theme');
        if (saved === 'dark' || saved === 'light') {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', saved);
        }
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      THESIS: A personal blog is the writing, not a concept wrapped around
      it — extended for a photography blog: the photo is the writing here,
      so the same restrained editorial world now serves the image first
      and the caption second, without inventing a new concept to do it.
      OWN-WORLD: Warm paper ground, near-black ink, a single reserved
      ink-blue accent used only for links and small labels. Fraunces for
      headlines (quiet personality, not loud), Newsreader serif for body
      reading, IBM Plex Mono only for dates/tags/credits. Hairline rules
      divide content instead of cards, shadows, or borders; photos carry
      no frame beyond their own edge.
      STORY: A visitor understands this is one person's photo journal,
      arranged chronologically; they scan a grid of covers, open an entry
      into its full photo (or short photo essay) with a short reflection
      below, and can see who keeps the journal on About. Any photo opens
      fullscreen on click, with a slideshow to step through every photo
      on that page.
      FIRST VIEWPORT: A plain text masthead (site name, two-link nav,
      unobtrusive light/dark switch) above a masonry grid of photo covers
      — image, title, date, tag — no card chrome, the photo's own edge is
      the only boundary.
      FORM: Canon/standing-exit world (Stripe Press / Stratechery
      register), extended rather than replaced: this is the "extend an
      existing surface" path — same tokens, new composition for image-led
      content, no new concept tournament run for a structural adaptation.
      FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends
      with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md.
    -->
    <slot />
    <Lightbox />
  </body>
</html>
